      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i know people say that, but it feels so superficial. like, \"go to therapy\" or \"take a vacation.\" a vacation is just moving the exhaustion to a different location. it doesn't change the fact that the machine keeps running and i'm just the part that's wearing out. everything feels so heavy and permanent. like i'm just waiting for something to finally just... stop. i feel like i've reached a point where there's no \"recharging\" anymore. there's just nothing left.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
