      "content": "It's true that the platitudes feel hollow when you're this deep in it, and that exhaustion is real. The idea of \"recharging\" is a myth when the core of the problem is the relentless pressure itself. If you feel like you're just waiting for it to stop, that's a very serious signal that you need a different kind of intervention than just a break. Please consider connecting with a crisis line or a doctor who can help you manage this intense feeling of hopelessness.",
